{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1373229-is-archspheres-really-a-\u201ctypo\u201d","id":1373229,"title":"Is Archspheres really a \u201ctypo\u201d?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-06T11:05:48-08:00","id":1373229,"title":"Is Archspheres really a \u201ctypo\u201d?","content":"First of all I just want to focus on this topic itself, so I won\u2019t mention the original authority even if somebody know him, it is meaningless. Thanks for your understanding.<br /> <br /> Well, I used to hear a statement from one of the major authorities of MtA\u2014Archspheres is a \u201ctypo\u201d:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Thanks, Lindsay and Pepsi. And no, no Arch-Spheres in M20.<br /> <br /> For one thing, the book is already colossal. Secondly, VERY few mages are supposed to know such Arts. Thirdly, they're game-wreckers for sure. And fourth, I wish they had never been done.<br /> <br /> The only reason Spheres go above Rank 5 at all is based in a typo in the very first Mage supplement, The Book of Chantries. In that book, one mage - Porthos, who at over 500 years old, was one of the most powerful mages in existence, - had Forces 6.<br /> <br /> The Book of Chantries was my first Mage project, written and developed amidst a storm of life-changing circumstances, not to mention my concurrent writing of the Black Furies Tribebook. Steve Brown had done the basic draft of Chantries, and I was rewriting it to bring my take on Mage to the line as well as to fill out Steve's initial ideas. Because Vampire had recently added Disciplines 6-10, Steve found it perfectly reasonable to assume that a five-centuries-old Archmage might have similar abilities. I didn't fix that reference, in large part because I was both preoccupied and unfamiliar with the Mage rules... which, to be fair, had existed for about ten weeks, total, at that time.<br /> <br /> Once I began delving into the Spheres, their power, and the ways in which they differed from Disciplines and Gifts (hint: They're a LOT more powerful, flexible, and open-ended), I decided that Spheres should never go about Rank 5. After all Rank 5 Effects allow you to create human life from nothing (Life 5/ Mind 5/ Spirit 5/ Prime 2), conjure atomic blasts (Forces 5/ Prime 5), disintegrate solid objects by making them unreal (Prime 5), create new souls (Spirit 5), and STACK PLACES ON TOP OF ONE ANOTHER (Correspondence 5). No vampire or werewolf can do that kind of shit, and so the Disciplines, Gifts (which go up only to 6) and Spheres are not even close to equivalent.<br /> <br /> But then, there was that damned Porthos with his Forces 5 in a published book. And so people kept asking, &quot;What can Forces 5 DO...?&quot;<br /> <br /> A few years later, after Mage 2nd had made the rules more workable than they had been in Mage 1, I did Horizon: Stronghold of Hope. In that book, Spheres went to 6 if you were incredibly old, unspeakably powerful, probably insane, and living in a Realm that allowed for gross distortions of Reality.<br /> <br /> So THEN, of course, everyone wanted Spheres 7-10.<br /> <br /> And I said No.<br /> <br /> And then I left the line, and folks both within and without <br /> <br /> White Wolf told Jesse to do a book with Arch-Spheres.<br /> <br /> So he did.<br /> <br /> And now, any young mage with enough experience points and a generous Storyteller can buy Forces 8 or something.<br /> <br /> In short, I hate the Arch-Spheres, but they were canon.<br /> I still have not yet decided what to do about that, but for that reason among many others, I was not going to put them in the main Mage 20 rulebook. </div> </div> </div>Most people accept this. But... at least on talking point, I think he is wrong, all of my evidence comes from 1st edition core.<br /> <br /> The most direct evidence is Lord Killavaro, a npc who has Force \u201c6\u201d:<br /> Page 289<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Spheres: Correspondence 3, Entropy 4, <b>Forces 6 (allows huge \u201cnatural\u201d disasters like earthquakes or volcanic eruptions),</b> </div> </div> </div>Some less direct but still obvious:<br /> Page 181<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It doesn\u2019t matter if the mage is traveling through the Realm of the Oracles of Time, which has a Sphere rating of <b>Time 8</b>. </div> </div> </div>Page 292<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wrinkle <b>(Time 5+)</b> </div> </div> </div>Even in the Sphere section they still imply the 6+ spheres may exist:<br /> Page 183<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only limitation on character is that some incredibly dramatic effects can only be performed by the Oracles, whose knowledge transcends the five ranks listed there. </div> </div> </div>Of course we all know this is archmage today, but after all it implies the 6+ spheres do exist.<br /> <br /> So I think Archspheres are not typo, most of authorities do have thinking about it, but they may not have a clear ideas about this","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T11:46:10-08:00","id":1373235,"title":"","content":"It's possible that the guy who wrote M1e was open to the notion of Spheres up to 10. But the whole line got handed over to Brucato immediately after that. And from then until he left White Wolf, Mage was what he said it was. <br /> <br /> There are a lot of things in M1e that never made it out of the core book and were revised away a year (?) later when M2e came out, if not sooner. And Sphere ratings above 5 are one of those things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T11:56:58-08:00","id":1373237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1373229-is-archspheres-really-a-\u201ctypo\u201d?p=1373235#post1373235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's possible that the guy who wrote M1e was open to the notion of Spheres up to 10. But the whole line got handed over to Brucato immediately after that. And from then until he left White Wolf, Mage was what he said it was.</div> </div> </div> </div>But I think he shouldn\u2019t use that absolute tongue, 1e core shows archspheres has been an idea despite clear or not. <br /> <br /> *Btw, I expect archmage book of M20... although they have said M20 won\u2019t concern this, but Book of Fallen do mention Archmage and Oracle","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T12:08:54-08:00","id":1373238,"title":"","content":"M20 is even more firmly \u201cwhatever Brucato says it is\u201d than even 2e was. As I understand it, there <i>won't</i> be an M20 supplement giving rules for the Arch-Spheres, just as there won't be one giving rules for Hedge Magic: you want either of these things, go get Horizon or Masters of the Art (whichever you prefer) for the Arch-Spheres stuff, or Sorcerer (whichever edition you prefer) for the Path Magic stuff. M20 and its official supplements aren't going to touch these areas. Storyteller's Vault is a different matter; but none of that is official.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T12:22:40-08:00","id":1373239,"title":"","content":"Haven't the Sphere descriptions in M20 pretty much taken in the capabilities of archspheres, assuming one racks up enough successes for the feat? I distinctly recall time travel now being possible with Time 5, though it's anything but easy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-06T14:09:24-08:00","id":1373257,"title":"","content":"There have been a few revisions to the Spheres between MRev and M20. But by and large, no; the Arch-Spheres haven't been folded into the Spheres. MRev already had Time Travel available at five dots \u2014 though, as you say, it was incredibly difficult. <br /> <br /> That said, it's worth noting that both Horizon and MotA are 2e supplements; and what 6 dots can do is compared to 2e's notion of wheat 5 dots can do. 2e put travel into the past firmly in the realm of the Oracles; MRev granted some limited access to it via Time 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-08T06:21:38-07:00","id":1373538,"title":"","content":"Time 5 in Revised core at least suggests that only Archmages can travel back in time.<br /> <br /> Time 5 in 2e could actually go back in time. In the Void Engineers Convention Book, the Chrononauts are said to go back and forward in Time and the Time 5 effect even tells you that they can, but due to bureaucracy and how dangerous the butterfly effect is, they don't tend to.<br /> <br /> As for the typo, who knows? Voormas had Entropy 6 in that book and the book of madness give archspheres for Medea and the Unnamed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25629-gghostwalker","name":"GGhostwalker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-09T04:03:45-07:00","id":1373723,"title":"","content":"Quite frankly, with M20 the Spheres at level 5 are so open-ended and flexible, there is no real *need* for Archspheres.<br /> All it takes is enough successes and creativity. Your Archmageness comes from your high Arete stat and dropped instruments - because I dare you to tell an Arete 8 Mage who can do most things without even needing to snap fingers, that they are 'Not a real Archmage'.<br /> Now, getting those tons of successes for the really godlike feats might be the hard part - and it *should be* - but technically there is no actual need for those 6+ Spheres.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-09T04:26:30-07:00","id":1373726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GGhostwalker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1373229-is-archspheres-really-a-\u201ctypo\u201d?p=1373538#post1373538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Time 5 in Revised core at least suggests that only Archmages can travel back in time.<br /> <br /> Time 5 in 2e could actually go back in time. In the Void Engineers Convention Book, the Chrononauts are said to go back and forward in Time and the Time 5 effect even tells you that they can, but due to bureaucracy and how dangerous the butterfly effect is, they don't tend to.<br /> <br /> As for the typo, who knows? Voormas had Entropy 6 in that book and the book of madness give archspheres for Medea and the Unnamed.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mentioned Medea and time travel, and my first thought was this: <a href=\"https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=PUaVsgtT230\" target=\"_blank\">https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=PUaVsgtT230</a> (I love Astronomy Club!).<br /> <br /> Who needs Time 6+ when you can steal a time machine?<br /> <br /> Sorry for the tangent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-09T04:40:02-07:00","id":1373728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GGhostwalker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1373229-is-archspheres-really-a-\u201ctypo\u201d?p=1373538#post1373538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the typo, who knows? Voormas had Entropy 6 in that book and the book of madness give archspheres for Medea and the Unnamed.</div> </div> </div> </div>My thought is the Porthos is the &quot;first&quot; npc in that book, and his Force 6 opened a rift on archspheres firstly, leading to 6-dot sphere of Voormas, Medea and Unnamed. That's the reason why he said this typo comes from him.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1373229-is-archspheres-really-a-\u201ctypo\u201d?p=1373723#post1373723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quite frankly, with M20 the Spheres at level 5 are so open-ended and flexible, there is no real *need* for Archspheres.</div> </div> </div> </div>But when you want to achieve something really epic? If you want to break the curse of caine or wyrm, how many masteries will you need?<br /> <br /> And to be honest I think simply accumulating success is still... have a top. They are not containing all","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 03-09-2020, 07:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-09T05:02:10-07:00","id":1373730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1373229-is-archspheres-really-a-\u201ctypo\u201d?p=1373728#post1373728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But when you want to achieve something really epic? If you want to break the curse of caine or wyrm, how many masteries will you need?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's entering Vampire/Werewolf Crossover-Land. Your Mage *literally* wants to beat capital-G GOD and/or one of the three fundamental forces of Reality itself. That's far beyond 'epic'.<br /> <br /> That's not a matter of a simple set of rolls - Archspheres or not - but should be the subject of a whole *campaign*, Storyteller fluff, perils, pitfalls, quests and absolutely epic achievements.<br /> <br /> If it was just a matter of having some Archspheres and doing enough rolls to literally beat God, that Mage also could singlehandedly end the Ascension War by themselves at any time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-09T05:26:30-07:00","id":1373740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1373229-is-archspheres-really-a-\u201ctypo\u201d?p=1373257#post1373257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There have been a few revisions to the Spheres between MRev and M20. But by and large, no; the Arch-Spheres haven't been folded into the Spheres. MRev already had Time Travel available at five dots \u2014 though, as you say, it was incredibly difficult.</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth to mention as another revision &quot;empowering&quot; Spheres in M20 it's that Life 5 in M20 can do perfect transformation of self AND others, while Revised allowed only self (and to affect others with the equivalent of Life 4 &quot;less than perfect&quot; shape changes).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-09T05:34:16-07:00","id":1373745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1373229-is-archspheres-really-a-\u201ctypo\u201d?p=1373730#post1373730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's entering Vampire/Werewolf Crossover-Land.</div> </div> </div> </div>No I just say transform a vampire/ wyrmish shapechanger into mundane one. Restoring vampire still needs Prime 6 in Revised<br /> <br /> And you must have enormous success to achieve devastating effects at 5 dots. When you just need 3+- success to nuke a city at 6 dots? I think they are necessary in some ways<br /> <br /> And even in the past breaking the whole curse of them do happen. Warrior-mage Yi laid the curse upon Kuei-Jin. But it\u2019s not my point","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-09T05:55:16-07:00","id":1373748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1373229-is-archspheres-really-a-\u201ctypo\u201d?p=1373745#post1373745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No I just say transform a vampire/ wyrmish shapechanger into mundane one. Restoring vampire still needs Prime 6 in Revised</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what Vampire ST handbook says - it's very much part of crossoverland.<br /> <br /> For Vampire, it makes a lota sense to have ArchMages with Spheres going to 6+ levels, as Vampire measures (and <i>compares</i>) powers in a scale from 1 to 10<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And you must have enormous success to achieve devastating effects at 5 dots. When you just need 3+- success to nuke a city at 6 dots? I think they are necessary in some ways<br /> <br /> And even in the past breaking the whole curse of them do happen. Warrior-mage Yi laid the curse upon Kuei-Jin. But it\u2019s not my point </div> </div> </div>It depends on what do you want Mages to be able to do. While Mage does sell magic(k) as being able to do everything, it never says it needs to be easy.<br /> <br /> If you just want ArchMages to get more &quot;bang&quot; for their successes, that could easily be modeled by giving special powers to Arete at the 6+ levels. Like to say that Mages with Arete 6 duplicate their successes. At 7 you can break the rule of targets and affect huge areas for free...and so on. etc.<br /> <br /> Archspheres (and even in 1e) represent a &quot;ceiling&quot; to what ordinary mages can do in a very similar vein as how Disciplines at 6+ represent in Vampire powers beyond the access of &quot;normal&quot; pc, but that can be reached in the course of play if the PC becomes an Elder. It allows you to build in the system &quot;Elder Mages&quot; of sorts.<br /> If you want to do that, it's a very convenient tool to have. But I think it stands to debate if one really needs &quot;Elder Mages&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-09-2020, 09:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T04:06:46-07:00","id":1374096,"title":"","content":"It almost certainly wasn't a typo I feel. Maybe a decision he regretted, but all the evidence suggests it's not a typo.<br /> <br /> Archspheres both Masters of the Art and Horizon felt a little ham fisted, part of me feels with recent editions stepping back from the &quot;You get 10 Arete and then you ascend&quot;, the Arete stat going above 10 feels a little more workable for a game than trying to invent new things for Spheres to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","name":"Distant Choir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T04:55:36-07:00","id":1374099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1373229-is-archspheres-really-a-\u201ctypo\u201d?p=1373748#post1373748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's what Vampire ST handbook says - it's very much part of crossoverland.<br /> <br /> For Vampire, it makes a lota sense to have ArchMages with Spheres going to 6+ levels, as Vampire measures (and <i>compares</i>) powers in a scale from 1 to 10<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It depends on what do you want Mages to be able to do. While Mage does sell magic(k) as being able to do everything, it never says it needs to be easy.<br /> <br /> If you just want ArchMages to get more &quot;bang&quot; for their successes, that could easily be modeled by giving special powers to Arete at the 6+ levels. Like to say that Mages with Arete 6 duplicate their successes. At 7 you can break the rule of targets and affect huge areas for free...and so on. etc.<br /> <br /> Archspheres (and even in 1e) represent a &quot;ceiling&quot; to what ordinary mages can do in a very similar vein as how Disciplines at 6+ represent in Vampire powers beyond the access of &quot;normal&quot; pc, but that can be reached in the course of play if the PC becomes an Elder. It allows you to build in the system &quot;Elder Mages&quot; of sorts.<br /> If you want to do that, it's a very convenient tool to have. But I think it stands to debate if one really needs &quot;Elder Mages&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I much prefer archspheres stopping at 6 actually.<br /> <br /> <br /> Level 7+ archspheres are just ridiculous<br /> For starters many of their higher ranked effects are not really &quot;stronger&quot; than the weaker archspheres. They just exist for the sake of filling out rank x<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In my opinion Level 6(and remember that in Horizon the costed around 120 xp i think) should basically be able to do everything EXCEPT the literally godlike<br /> Creating an entire universe or an entirely new force, or complete immortality come to mind....<br /> This should remain the province of the Exemplars or something like that.<br /> (Not oracles, since they are not supposed to be obsessed with the archspheres)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T05:06:04-07:00","id":1374101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Distant Choir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1373229-is-archspheres-really-a-\u201ctypo\u201d?p=1374096#post1374096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It almost certainly wasn't a typo I feel.</div> </div> </div> </div>But I think he shouldn\u2019t say it\u2019s a typo, no it isn\u2019t, everything show authorities do consider this<br /> <br /> Another thing I feel much more incredible is, everyone I encountered treat his story as golden rule, simply accept it and don\u2019t even think about it. No one come out to correct this. And his lore is just a rootless tree very easy to wipe out. Jesus","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 03-11-2020, 09:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T08:18:55-07:00","id":1374137,"title":"","content":"Indeed, &quot;typo&quot; it's most likely the wrong word.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1373229-is-archspheres-really-a-\u201ctypo\u201d?p=1374099#post1374099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">stuff</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm mostly of the same opinion.<br /> <br /> I like a lot of the new concepts MotA brought on the table for high level mages, but certainly the Archsphere layout up to 10 it's flawed. The effects they offer and the system they give for them it's often so closed, contained and complete that some feel more like &quot;super Rotes&quot; than actual Spheres of influence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T10:47:13-07:00","id":1374168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1373229-is-archspheres-really-a-\u201ctypo\u201d?p=1374101#post1374101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I think he shouldn\u2019t say it\u2019s a typo, no it isn\u2019t, everything show authorities do consider this<br /> <br /> Another thing I feel much more incredible is, everyone I encountered treat his story as golden rule, simply accept it and don\u2019t even think about it. No one come out to correct this. And his lore is just a rootless tree very easy to wipe out. Jesus</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, the tone between 2e and m20 is so different even though it's predominantly the same writer.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, what do we think a good version of Archspheres should be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","name":"Distant Choir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-11T10:58:40-07:00","id":1374170,"title":"","content":"I personally agree that the Archsphere system in the Horizon book is better than the one in Masters Of The Art. A single new level 6 that enhances and boosts the sphere's normal effects by a great deal.<br /> It would need some subtle rewriting for things like the Life sphere, because in M20 it allows full Metamorphosis on others at 5 already, and the Time sphere because M20 allows backward travel at 5 already as well - but for the most part the Horizon system just works, and it works fine in the way that it simply takes the previous sphere levels and turbocharges them by essentially allowing for the same extreme godlike feats, just with with less successes required.<br /> It's simple, elegant, powerful, has a deserving cost, and just 'fits' into the normal sphere system without actually limiting the previous existing levels through its existence. Again, unlike the MOTA system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 03-11-2020, 02:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T04:52:36-07:00","id":1374323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1373229-is-archspheres-really-a-\u201ctypo\u201d?p=1374170#post1374170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally agree that the Archsphere system in the Horizon book is better than the one in Masters Of The Art. A single new level 6 that enhances and boosts the sphere's normal effects by a great deal.<br /> It would need some subtle rewriting for things like the Life sphere, because in M20 it allows full Metamorphosis on others at 5 already, and the Time sphere because M20 allows backward travel at 5 already as well - but for the most part the Horizon system just works, and it works fine in the way that it simply takes the previous sphere levels and turbocharges them by essentially allowing for the same extreme godlike feats, just with with less successes required.<br /> It's simple, elegant, powerful, has a deserving cost, and just 'fits' into the normal sphere system without actually limiting the previous existing levels through its existence. Again, unlike the MOTA system.</div> </div> </div> </div>My personal interpretation of time 5 time travel is that you can &quot;look but not touch'. Similar to the Dur an ki ritual that transports you back in time. You can not use it to truly alter time but you CAN use it to get a personal interview of Cicero or read the first bible ever writter<br /> <br /> <br /> So with M20 life 5 i can transform someone into an ant instead of more-or-less equal mass animal?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T05:12:19-07:00","id":1374329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1373229-is-archspheres-really-a-\u201ctypo\u201d?p=1374323#post1374323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Similar to the Dur an ki ritual that transports you back in time. </div> </div> </div> </div>Which one? <br /> <br /> Sorry, but to be honest I dislike the blood magic rules which is very overpowered, they\u2019re vampiric sphere magick. A blood magician which many level 5 paths and rituals can even override a master with many level 5 spheres","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T05:23:43-07:00","id":1374333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1373229-is-archspheres-really-a-\u201ctypo\u201d?p=1374323#post1374323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So with M20 life 5 i can transform someone into an ant instead of more-or-less equal mass animal?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. <br /> <br /> Before that was a function of lvl 6 Life. Which kinda made sense with how the Sphere was built (affecting yourself first, others the next level).<br /> <br /> But w/o lvl 6 Spheres, it was a gross limitation for the supposedly &quot;limitless&quot; potential of magic(k). Since M20 wanted to get rid of ArchSpheres it makes a lot of sense to fold that into the 5th level<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T07:20:13-07:00","id":1374343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1373229-is-archspheres-really-a-\u201ctypo\u201d?p=1374323#post1374323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My personal interpretation of time 5 time travel is that you can &quot;look but not touch'. Similar to the Dur an ki ritual that transports you back in time. You can not use it to truly alter time but you CAN use it to get a personal interview of Cicero or read the first bible ever writter</div> </div> </div> </div>In M20? Nah, Time 5 allows proper travelling back in time. Howeverrrrrr it (probably very intentionally) does not talk about the concepts and theories of multiple timelines, branching possibilities etc.<br /> I think the VE's mention Everett Volumes though.<br /> <br /> I think it's very very safe to say that the past of a current timeline can't be changed - else a random powerful Mage could literally undo everything.<br /> However, it even allows for further thought experiments.<br /> <br /> Consider a Mage that drops an anchor in their current time, travels back, does things, and travels forward again to the anchor - nothing will have changed! How strange!<br /> <br /> Meanwhile a Mage that travels back without an anchor, then changes things and travels back to their own time finds that their efforts of change were successful! Yay! Triumph!<br /> ....while their friends keep on waiting for their return in their original timeline. Weeks later, the Mage is labeled as MIA, and will be dearly missed by friends and family. The end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T08:05:00-07:00","id":1374349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1373229-is-archspheres-really-a-\u201ctypo\u201d?p=1374333#post1374333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yup.<br /> <br /> Before that was a function of lvl 6 Life. Which kinda made sense with how the Sphere was built (affecting yourself first, others the next level).<br /> <br /> But w/o lvl 6 Spheres, it was a gross limitation for the supposedly &quot;limitless&quot; potential of magic(k). Since M20 wanted to get rid of ArchSpheres it makes a lot of sense to fold that into the 5th level<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, am not sure if this is really overpowered to be honest. Sure, you can squash a bug, but you could also use these 5(for the duration of one turn), to deal a good amount of damage, that would kill or cripple most unprepared beings. Not to mention that &quot;rip the man-body&quot; is a much easier effect. <br /> <br /> Maybe i would even allow normal-sized transformation of others at life 4. It does seem to be a stable of witchcraft of legends<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> For that matter maybe life 3 should also allow you to heal others of aggravated damage....Maybe it cheapens aggravated damage, but (among other people) it never made sense for technomancers in my opinion<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">By the way, i just remembered another reason that level 7 + archspheres are bad... apparently i think you need life 7 to create a virus... such as the common cold... Could be wrong though</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">In M20? Nah, Time 5 allows proper travelling back in time. Howeverrrrrr it (probably very intentionally) does not talk about the concepts and theories of multiple timelines, branching possibilities etc.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I think the VE's mention Everett Volumes though.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I think it's very very safe to say that the past of a current timeline can't be changed - else a random powerful Mage could literally undo everything.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">However, it even allows for further thought experiments.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Consider a Mage that drops an anchor in their current time, travels back, does things, and travels forward again to the anchor - nothing will have changed! How strange!</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Meanwhile a Mage that travels back without an anchor, then changes things and travels back to their own time finds that their efforts of change were successful! Yay! Triumph!</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">....while their friends keep on waiting for their return in their original timeline. Weeks later, the Mage is labeled as MIA, and will be dearly missed by friends and family. The end.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> To be honest i am not sure about how different timelines should work. Are they subservient to the &quot;main timeline&quot;? Does the concept of a main timeline even make sense from a physics perspective?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Which one?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Sorry, but to be honest I dislike the blood magic rules which is very overpowered, they\u2019re vampiric sphere magick. A blood magician which many level 5 paths and rituals can even override a master with many level 5 spheres</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>I believe it's called turning back the sky. Hey, it's a level 7 ritual with a lot of strings attached so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T08:31:48-07:00","id":1374354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1373229-is-archspheres-really-a-\u201ctypo\u201d?p=1374343#post1374343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the VE's mention Everett Volumes though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both VE and Etherites Revised mentions them. BUT, both make very major distinctions between traveling to an Everett Volume and what Time 5 does.<br /> <br /> Traveling to an Everett Volume requires more magic(k) than just Time 5. You need Entropy 4 at least. More importantly, it causes less Paradox than using Time 5:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VE</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Void Engineers might use them for <b>a less risky form of time travel, albeit one with fewer practical benefits</b>. Changing history in an Everett Volume doesn\u2019t affect the main timeline, but it won\u2019t invoke disastrous temporal paradoxes either</div> </div> </div> </div>Which strongly implies that *arch* Time Travel has *more practical benefits* changing history at the cost of epic Paradoxes<br /> <br /> That's not to say that the current timeline necessarily can be changed with Time 5 <b>in M20</b>.<br /> <br /> Since Revised Time 5 time travel kills you, stories were safe. No need to apply the same rules in 20th edition where this it's allowed for *regular* characters. Ultimately it depends on the ST.<br /> <br /> However...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Consider a Mage that drops an anchor in their current time, travels back, does things, and travels forward again to the anchor - nothing will have changed! How strange! </div> </div> </div>In M20 it's simply not true that &quot;nothing changed&quot;...because remember that RAW, while not insta-death, <i>you still eat a fuckton of Paradox</i> for your &quot;nothing happened&quot;. Now, &quot;strange&quot; it's not the words *I* would be thinking...<br /> <br /> If you don't want to narrate a Time Travel story because it's problematic, just say that Time Travel it's pc forbbiden. Or at the very least make it Coincident (or &quot;normal Vulgar&quot; rather than super-duper-extra-Vulgar) if it's going to be pointless (or just &quot;perception&quot; based).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 03-12-2020, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T08:41:00-07:00","id":1374356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">By the way, i just remembered another reason that level 7 + archspheres are bad... apparently i think you need life 7 to create a virus... such as the common cold... Could be wrong though</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's <b>8</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T16:03:48-07:00","id":1374445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1373229-is-archspheres-really-a-\u201ctypo\u201d?p=1374349#post1374349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For that matter maybe life 3 should also allow you to heal others of aggravated damage....</div> </div> </div> </div>I... thought it <i>does</i>, but you just have to spend Quintessence to make the effect work on aggravated damage? So far as I recall, Life 3 has always been the sphere rating needed for healing other people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T17:35:52-07:00","id":1374459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1373229-is-archspheres-really-a-\u201ctypo\u201d?p=1374445#post1374445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I... thought it <i>does</i>, but you just have to spend Quintessence to make the effect work on aggravated damage? So far as I recall, Life 3 has always been the sphere rating needed for healing other people.</div> </div> </div> </div>haven;t checked for a while, but i think you need life 4 to heal aggravated damage on others. Life 3 to heal them of other types of damage","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T23:49:05-07:00","id":1374514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1373229-is-archspheres-really-a-\u201ctypo\u201d?p=1374445#post1374445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I... thought it <i>does</i>, but you just have to spend Quintessence to make the effect work on aggravated damage? So far as I recall, Life 3 has always been the sphere rating needed for healing other people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, in Revised it was Life 4. And the Verbena Revised Handbook gave that Tradition the speshul ability to heal others with Life 3 already - if it is bashing damage.<br /> <br /> There was a Mage Revised FAQ later that somehow says 'As implied with the writeup of Life 3 you can heal others with it', but I think whoever answered that question in the FAQ completely missed the Life 4 and Verbena writeup somehow, as both of those directly contradict that.<br /> <br /> On that note, I'm glad M20 moved that back down to Life 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 03-13-2020, 02:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T07:14:08-07:00","id":1374560,"title":"","content":"I think a lot of what Horizon's Archspheres suggested were quite interesting, but Time 6's ability to go back in time was something you could do at 5 dots in the VE book that came out the same year(and otherwise wasn't suggested to be a special rule) and the whole Spirit 6's abilities were...laughable, really. Sure it sounds interesting in theory that you need 25+ successes to compel an Incarna or Celestine to do a very simple task you...until you realise it's a Willpower roll that isn't an extended action, so you'd need Mind in excess to add bonus dice to the pool.<br /> <br /> <br /> I feel a combination of Horizon's Archsphere feat improving and MoTA's Forces 6 double successes sense could work well for pretty much any edition outside of M20. In M20's case, you'd just need something like the MoTA forces 6 thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","name":"Distant Choir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T12:20:59-07:00","id":1374608,"title":"","content":"Personally, I don't feel a lot of need to add Sphere levels just to add &quot;extra strenght&quot; to magick.<br /> <br /> In general, the number of successes determines the strength of the magick, and that it's a function of Arete. I can see why some would want ArchMages to do the same with less effort (as MotA Forces 6 trully adds nothing to the concept of Forces, it's just a &quot;multiplier&quot;), but I just can't call that a &quot;Sphere level&quot;.<br /> <br /> Spheres are &quot;spheres of influence&quot;. And while it's not entirely correct to say levels don't add power, each <i>level </i>always change radically what you can do and what you can affect. The impossible becomes possible. MotA Forces 6 doesn't do this: I can do everything that Forces 6 can do with Forces 5, it will just take me twice the time. <hr />As far as ArchSpheres go, this is my opinion:<br /> <br /> One line that I loved of MotA was how they described Archspheres effects as &quot;<i>stories</i>&quot; (there are no Rotes for powers this grand). How could *that* work?<br /> <br /> Of course, MotA then goes and butchers this idea by providing some Sphere levels so closed in what they do, that they're practically Rotes: They even have the same &quot;format&quot; as Rotes (fluff <i>and </i>System, rather than only fluff like Spheres).<br /> <br /> I honestly don't think that having a spell that allows to cast with successes *2 or does *one* thing like Awakeening someone can be called <b><i>a story</i></b>. It can be used as <i>mcguffing </i>of a story, sure, but so can lvl 5 Sphere effects. Except that lvl 6+ can be put out of the reach of the players. But, ultimately, if they were intended as game-breaking <i>mcguffin </i>effects outside players, why limit them with rules?, why limit STs when WoD always assigns <i>narrative</i>(AKA. undefined)<i> powers</i> to their mcguffing characters?. Better say 6 it's narrative in that case: In a scale of 1 to 5, Porthos has a 6 - of course he can do that.<br /> <br /> The concept of &quot;replace effect with story&quot; it's, I think, very well represented by one crossover module: The Red Sign. It deals with reversing the Curse of Caine. But rather than giving you a Rote with a System and telling you: &quot;you need to be this <s>tall</s> powerful to cast this effect&quot;, and then ask you to build successes in a generic ritual, the story explores various different paths that could be taken in order to perform the feat.<br /> <br /> Abeit this module <i>barely </i>involves Archspheres (only *implied* to be a thing by the Yellow Sign Grimoire), it's still interesting on the grounds the whole story it's basically the casting of a big effect, and thus it shows that it can be done.<br /> <br /> Now, the module involves a lot of &quot;mckguffing hunt&quot; and ST fiat, and that's not very Spherical...but I think that focusing on that would be missing the forest for the trees. Ultimately, all this setup <i>needs </i>it's for ArchMagic(k) 1\u00ba to exist (as to justify that magick can, indeed, do the impossible - if only at some nebulous, ordinarily unreachable, level) and 2\u00ba to be something more involved than the ordinary Rote.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, I think that magic(k) that *does the impossible* can be modeled this way.<br /> <br /> Now, as much as I criticize ArchSpheres, MotA introduces some very neat concepts. To mention some:<br /> *Metapatters it's a whole new thing, much closer in concept to &quot;platonic ideas&quot; than ordinary patters...that these *exist* has very interesting ramifications (what can be learnt by studying, say, the MetaPattern of Vampires in a city?), that, of couse, MotA reduces to a *bonus* w/o exploring it further.<br /> *Entropy 8 it's the only time in all of Mage where resurrection it's adressed in a way that's 100% compatible with Wraith. Everyone uses Life (obvious) + Spirit to resurrect by forcing the spirit back to the body: but what if there's *no* spirit left?, what if the person, like most people as per Wraith, has been devoured by Oblivion or hasn't left anything like a ghost?. The ideas of having to &quot;fish&quot; and stich together the fragments of the soul lost in the Tempest and to &quot;bring life from Oblivion&quot; adresses this (and dealing directly with these supernatural powers it's also a &quot;new concept&quot; rather than a mere bonus, I think).<br /> *Time 6+ it's mostly &quot;time travel&quot;, but it does allow some interesting shenanigans connecting timelines. And I think the idea that there's a point in time that's like the Correspondence point it's interesting, albeit the applications seem nonexistent - the very &quot;spell&quot; states it's useless for the mage who casts it.<br /> *Mind 6+ brings the idea (that was already on Horizon) of messsing with the &quot;collective subconscious&quot;. That adds a whole new dimension to mind (one level before that either didn't existed, or was just a fancy name for the Astral Umbra).It's also not very explored. Also opens the memories and &quot; mind&quot; of the Avatar. Albeit, again, nothing of this it's very explored<br /> <br /> And so on...<br /> <br /> I can even see some of these involving stories in and of themselves: Going to fish the pieces of a soul can be a story, for instance.<br /> <br /> The main reason to have Spheres above 5 it's to have a level of power that *can't* be reached ordinarily, but that could be used as a road to permit powers outside the normal rules. As Dataweaver says, lvl 6 as a mckguffin level that PCs can't reach while being PC seems the way to go to me.<br /> <br /> In a similar vein, I could see this Arete x 2 successes as the result of a mage actually *studying the universe* and discovering some power or entity that can be abused to increase her own &quot;magical potential&quot;.<br /> Like, perhaps if you transform yourself into a living nexus of power with Forces 5/Corr 5/Spirit 5/Prime 5 to connect your Avatar to the pulsatic core of the Shade Realm of Forces, then you can do that &quot;metamagick effect&quot; of Forces 6 (with whatever consequences the ST deems appropiate to such an esoteric transformation, including maybe painful death if your body it's merely human). And the travel to &quot;the pulsating core of the Shade Realm&quot; would be a story...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T13:51:25-07:00","id":1374630,"title":"","content":"This. <br /> <br /> Personally, I'd adapt heavily from <b>Mage: the Awakening</b>'s supplement <b>Imperial Mysteries</b>: not so much the 6+ dot levels (though there's stuff in there that might be worth considering) or the stuff that's specific to <b>Awakening</b>'s cosmology (e.g., Golden Roads and the Supernal Realms); but things like Imperial Spell Factors (i.e., a way to amp up the effectiveness of the successes that an Archmaster achieves) and Acts of Imperium (detailed in the Appendix, and basically built around the notion of \u201carchmagic as story\u201d that <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> just mentioned), and possibly even the notion that arch-magic costs the equivalent of experience points to use, making it something that even Archmasters use sparingly. (This isn't that different from how the creation of certain Wonders requires an expenditure of Willpower dots, which then require experience points to recover). <br /> <br /> It even has the notion that arch-mastery isn't merely a result of spending enough experience points for a sixth dot but is a sort of \u201csecond Awakening\u201d, although the implementation found in <b>Imperial Mysteries</b> ties heavily into <b>Awakening</b>'s metaphysics and would require substantial reworking before it could be applied to <b>Ascension</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T18:25:09-07:00","id":1374849,"title":"","content":"As far as I'm concerned the Horizon: Stronghold of Hope book is the only glimpse we need of Archspheres. They represent the epic levels those spheres can be used much like Elder Disciplines were originally supposed to be treated (until they got more codified and those examples were treated as strict levels). Personally, I'm more interested in seeing if there's some different perspective the Technocracy or Nephandi have of other spheres as that's at least paradigm based with limited mechanical differences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The only consistent wisdom is in knowing you know nothing&quot; ~ Socrates <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1197-imthestein","name":"Imthestein","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1197_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-15T05:16:51-07:00","id":1374904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1373229-is-archspheres-really-a-\u201ctypo\u201d?p=1374630#post1374630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry guy, but do you know how to wash away permanent paradox in M20? Horizon book doesn't mention it, Masters of the Art needs Prime 9 (nigh-impossible, only the greatest Oracle or Exampler can have, if they do exist), M20 says you can't and I haven't found any inaccessible way. I think it may need Prime 5 and tons of successes (20 / permandox?)<br /> <br /> If you can use Prime 5 to wash it, I think many powerful mages won't retreat to Umbra","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-15T08:27:15-07:00","id":1374923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1373229-is-archspheres-really-a-\u201ctypo\u201d?p=1374904#post1374904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry guy, but do you know how to wash away permanent paradox in M20? Horizon book doesn't mention it, Masters of the Art needs Prime 9 (nigh-impossible, only the greatest Oracle or Exampler can have, if they do exist), M20 says you can't and I haven't found any inaccessible way. I think it may need Prime 5 and tons of successes (20 / permandox?)<br /> <br /> If you can use Prime 5 to wash it, I think many powerful mages won't retreat to Umbra</div> </div> </div> </div>There is an area in the umbra(actually mentioned in masters of the art) that removes paradox... with a lot of damage. I am not sure how it's called. I think it's Flux?<br /> <br /> A kind storyteller might also allow prime 5 to temporarily suppress permanent paradox, but it should NEVER be able to remove it all.(else, all the old masters would have done so already)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-15T08:58:57-07:00","id":1374929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1373229-is-archspheres-really-a-\u201ctypo\u201d?p=1374608#post1374608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Snip</div> </div> </div> </div>I just want to say that I think lots of the ideas here as presented are quite interesting. I'd also so they're not mutually exclusive with the mystic senses of forces 6 and doubling successes. When it comes down to it, the usage of an ability even in regular MtA is still a story, even disbarring results. You have to come up with the idea, make it work within your paradigm, set aside a space to do it, set up a few precautions in doing it. Then you're subjected to a roll where for better or worse you could still fail (even with doubled successes). And then you deal with the potential consequences of even a successful casting of that ritual (What did your rivals think of that? What does Unbelief think of that? How does that change your approach?). You might then say that you could do this with Forces 5 for example, it's just slightly harder. Maybe. But your character is an Archmage now, and your inclination / aptitude at bringing these new mythical effects into being is in it of itself a complication that a normal master might not experience. <br /> <br /> Another sticking point for me personally, and this probably is just a me-and-three-people-I-know-thing, but I kind of hate it when ability is left explicitly as being a plot device, especially if a player wants to use it. Spheres, as freeform as they are, still have a basis and system you can use at each rank. It sort of ruins the flow of the story if you're trying to get in there and then you immediately recognise something as a plot device. Not my cup of tea. <br /> <br /> You're totally right about them introducing new concepts but then deciding not to...well...explore them, which is something a hypothetical archmage supplement should do. I want to know more about this 'sub realm' of time that it's sometimes mentioned in the Time 1 Sense. I want to know what is it about Life Patterns that makes their flow of raw quintessence so interesting? MoTA did a rather excellent job at talking about what potential stories / complications come with being an Archmage, and I feel it could go a step further. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1373229-is-archspheres-really-a-\u201ctypo\u201d?p=1374630#post1374630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Snip</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not too familiar with Awakening or it's cosmology, but I kind of feel this suggestion does a dis-service to both what an Archmage is and what an Oracle is. Archmages are ultimately still attainable / real figures that if you had the know how and connections could walk up to them and talk (albeit perhaps dealing with their wonderfully designated Quiet or hundreds of years of grumpy). They lead political factions and they're still, most of the time, human beings with a very honed perspective. They're attained great power and sometimes great wisdom, but ultimately that does not an Ascension make.<br /> <br /> A second awakening type thing for Archmages doesn't really make sense, considering if anything most editions post 1e posit that attaining power to this level draws one away from Ascension. A second awakening should be the province of the Oracles, totally mystical and often apocryphal figures that try to encourage others to attaining actual Ascension. And they know what Ascension is or at least how to 'do' it. They have even greater political power of Archmages if they wished to use it, but they don't. <br /> <br /> And again, perhaps it's just a me thing, but I find using XP as an actual resource for things like casting a spell feels kind of bad in play, especially since most of the rules are rather lax on XP (unlike in Exalted). The consequences of trying to cast, failing to cast or succeeding to cast should be the main focal point, not something so gameified as XP. <br /> <br /> <br /> Just to reiterate, these are just personal musings of mine, and I think both your ideas are rather interesting. I also think it's a good exercise to hone our ideas in an open forum like this, either from critique or articulating our own thoughts :P<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","name":"Distant Choir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-15T11:44:30-07:00","id":1374949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1373229-is-archspheres-really-a-\u201ctypo\u201d?p=1374904#post1374904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry guy, but do you know how to wash away permanent paradox in M20? Horizon book doesn't mention it, Masters of the Art needs Prime 9 (nigh-impossible, only the greatest Oracle or Exampler can have, if they do exist), M20 says you can't and I haven't found any inaccessible way. I think it may need Prime 5 and tons of successes (20 / permandox?)<br /> <br /> If you can use Prime 5 to wash it, I think many powerful mages won't retreat to Umbra</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm brain farting on what book it's in, but someone here will surely recall, that the only way of shedding Perma Dox is by going to the Umbra and using a Prime (5?) Ritual to shed it on a 1 for 1 basis with your Avatar.<br /> <br /> Needless to say reducing your Avatar Rating to shed Perma Dox is quite an expensive price to pay, but since they are basically fused together there is no other way.<br /> <br /> Quite frankly I've always liked it that the price is so high. Anything else would make Perma Dox and paradox in general even less meaningful than it already is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T22:25:50-07:00","id":1375222,"title":"","content":"I get the feeling its not a typo, It just seems some wished it was a typo but it doesn't appear to be a typo.<br /> <br /> Seems confusing with so much fluff about Archmages and Oracles but them not supposed to exist. Headache city. The Imperial Mysteries crew were really good with their Archmage Crunch and Fluff though I'm thinking of touching upon that along with the older rules to portray it in my games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T22:56:58-07:00","id":1375224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1373229-is-archspheres-really-a-\u201ctypo\u201d?p=1375222#post1375222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get the feeling its not a typo, It just seems some wished it was a typo but it doesn't appear to be a typo.</div> </div> </div> </div>The OP is correct that the original, 1st edition book contains hints that Stewart Wieck was thinking in terms of there being ten levels to the Spheres, with the idea that the details of those Spheres would be worked out later. <br /> <br /> It was the only book in the entire line until Initiates of the Art that Brucato had nothing to do with. For the next five years, Brucato shaped Mage. He <i>started</i> by taking the glorious mess that was 1e and beating it into some semblance of a viable game. That frequently entailed throwing out or reinterpreting things that didn't work; and the idea that there were more than 5 levels to the Spheres was something he eventually came to the conclusion was a bad idea \u2014 but not before a book made it into print that had six dots on the character sheet under one of the Spheres. Brucato has referred to it as a typo; I think \u201coversight\u201d or \u201cmistake\u201d might have been a better description of what he was trying to say. <br /> <br /> 1e doesn't trump literally everything that came out over the next five years; and what the original writer was thinking doesn't matter as much as what the subsequent line editor did with the game. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1373229-is-archspheres-really-a-\u201ctypo\u201d?p=1375222#post1375222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems confusing with so much fluff about Archmages and Oracles but them not supposed to exist. Headache city. The Imperial Mysteries crew were really good with their Archmage Crunch and Fluff though I'm thinking of touching upon that along with the older rules to portray it in my games.</div> </div> </div> </div> If I recall correctly, one of the guys who wrote Imperial Mysteries was also involved in writing Masters of the Art, which is why many of the concepts that MotA introduced resurfaced in IM.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-16T23:27:39-07:00","id":1375228,"title":"","content":"Let me elaborate a bit: in M1e, p.181, there's reference to the \u201cRealm of the Oracles of Time\u201d, which is said to have a Sphere rating of Time 8. On that same page, there's mention that Realms have ratings on all none Spheres, with Earth being 0 in everything, and a two-dimensional Really (such as in the book \u201cFlatland\u201d) might have a Correspondence rating of -4. As far as I know, this business of Realms having Sphere ratings that determine what is and isn't magical in them is something that got tossed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-17T01:21:30-07:00","id":1375237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1373229-is-archspheres-really-a-\u201ctypo\u201d?p=1375224#post1375224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">He </span></span><i>started </i><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">by taking the glorious mess that was 1e and beating it into some semblance of a viable game. </span></span></div> </div> </div> </div> </div>This, I used to hear that Mage 1e book was originally inviable and finally became accessible after the Players' Guide, Book of Shadow (additionally, why Players' Guide has only one edition... of course some sourcebooks of M20 are its &quot;Players' Guide&quot; in some ways...)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1373229-is-archspheres-really-a-\u201ctypo\u201d?p=1375224#post1375224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I recall correctly, one of the guys who wrote Imperial Mysteries was also involved in writing Masters of the Art, which is why many of the concepts that MotA introduced resurfaced in IM.</div> </div> </div> </div>Malcolm Sheppard. He even has account on this Forum","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}